.idea/
__pycache__/

# Anchored. The operator's real configuration is the one at the repo root; unanchored,
# this also swallowed examples/auto_toggle/config.json — the tracked golden fixture.
/config.json
# Anchored and directory-only. A bare `data` also matches a *file* named data and any
# nested data/ directory (tests/data/, docker/data/). Public example data lives in
# examples/, which is tracked — see examples/README.md.
/data/

# .env.example is tracked; the real .env holds the MQTT and InfluxDB credentials
.env
.gstack/

# Machine-specific tooling permissions — regenerated per machine, meaningless to anyone
# else. The Motrix Edge View repo ignores exactly this file for the same reason, while
# tracking .claude/launch.json beside it because that one is how a contributor starts the
# dev server.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Defence in depth. virtualenv, pytest and ruff each write a self-ignoring `*` into the
# directory they create, so these three lines change nothing today — they matter only if
# something ever produces one of these without that file.
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# A plugin from someone else's repository is vendored into an axis directory, and it is
# the operator's, not ours: `git status` stays clean and `git pull` never conflicts with
# it. Anchored and directory-only, like the rules above — no shipped axis has a
# sub-directory, so these match nothing in this tree today and everything an operator
# adds. (`__pycache__/` above already covers the axis caches; this simply also does.)
# A fork that genuinely wants to commit a vendored plugin uses `git add -f`.
/connectors/*/
/devices/*/
/algorithms/*/
/storage/*/
/services/*/
